{{also|Dividend}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|frm|dividende|}}, from {{uder|en|la|dividendum||thing to be divided}}, future passive participle of {{m|la|divido||to divide}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪvɪdɛnd/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-dividend.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|finance}} A [[cash]] [[payment]] of [[money]] by a [[company]] to its [[shareholder]]s, usually made [[periodically]] (e.g., [[quarterly]] or [[annually]]).
# {{lb|en|arithmetic}} A number or [[expression]] that is to be divided by another.
#: ''In "42 ÷ 3" the '''dividend''' is the 42.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} [[beneficial|Beneficial]] [[result]]s from a [[metaphorical]] [[investment]] (of [[time]], [[effort]], etc.)
#: ''His 10,000 hours of practice and recitals eventually paid '''dividends''' when he become first-chair violinist.''
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Retribution|https://books.google.com/books?isbn=1426878931|author=Cameron Haley |year=2012|passage=That blood and pain paid a '''dividend''', too, even when the subject wasn't a sorcerer.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Slow Burn: Dead Fire, Book 4:|https://books.google.com/books?isbn=1499118910|author=Bobby Adair |year=2014|passage=The money I'd spent on getting scuba certified was about to pay a dividend. My half-baked escape plan came together.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=The Beauties and Furies|page=163|https://books.google.com/books?isbn=1925410137|author=Christina Stead |year=2016|passage='Why not: you, Elvira, will shortly pay a '''dividend''', that is, have a child.'}}

